IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `efma-foreign-employee`

-- Employment of Foreign Manpower Act 1990 (with regs 2(3), 17, 18 and the Seventh Schedule of the Work Passes
-- Regulations 2012) -- the foreign employee's questions, worked cases.
--
-- SEAT: the foreign employee. Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law.
-- Nothing here has been checked against a decided case, a levy order or a work pass condition (none were deposited).
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table of which facts are set (scratchpad
-- gen_employment-of-foreign-manpower-act-1990_baseline.py). Expected results were written by hand from the text;
-- several are the hand-checked values of the first-pass encoding (naive-2026-10), re-derived here against the
-- deposited text.

§ `Fixtures`

`a foreign worker` MEANS `Me` WITH
    `my standing` IS `neither a citizen nor a permanent resident`
    `I seek, have been offered or am in employment in Singapore` IS TRUE
    `I am employed under a contract of service` IS TRUE
    `I engage or seek to engage in a trade, vocation or profession` IS FALSE
    `I engage or seek to engage in another activity in Singapore for gain` IS FALSE
    `the Minister has specified by Gazette notification a class I belong to as foreign employees` IS FALSE

`a permanent resident at work` MEANS `Me` WITH
    `my standing` IS `a permanent resident of Singapore`
    `I seek, have been offered or am in employment in Singapore` IS TRUE
    `I am employed under a contract of service` IS TRUE
    `I engage or seek to engage in a trade, vocation or profession` IS FALSE
    `I engage or seek to engage in another activity in Singapore for gain` IS FALSE
    `the Minister has specified by Gazette notification a class I belong to as foreign employees` IS FALSE

`a foreign freelance designer` MEANS `Me` WITH
    `my standing` IS `neither a citizen nor a permanent resident`
    `I seek, have been offered or am in employment in Singapore` IS FALSE
    `I am employed under a contract of service` IS FALSE
    `I engage or seek to engage in a trade, vocation or profession` IS TRUE
    `I engage or seek to engage in another activity in Singapore for gain` IS FALSE
    `the Minister has specified by Gazette notification a class I belong to as foreign employees` IS FALSE

`my valid pass` MEANS `My work pass` WITH
    `I hold a work pass issued to me` IS TRUE
    `the pass names as my employer the person I work for` IS TRUE
    `the work is in the trade, sector, occupation or type of employment specified in the pass or submitted in the application` IS TRUE
    `if the Controller has approved me to engage in this other work` IS FALSE
    `the period specified in the pass has not ended` IS TRUE
    `the Controller has suspended or revoked the pass` IS FALSE
    `the Controller has cancelled the pass on application` IS FALSE
    `my immigration pass has expired without renewal or been cancelled` IS FALSE

`a pass naming another employer` MEANS `My work pass` WITH
    `I hold a work pass issued to me` IS TRUE
    `the pass names as my employer the person I work for` IS FALSE
    `the work is in the trade, sector, occupation or type of employment specified in the pass or submitted in the application` IS TRUE
    `if the Controller has approved me to engage in this other work` IS FALSE
    `the period specified in the pass has not ended` IS TRUE
    `the Controller has suspended or revoked the pass` IS FALSE
    `the Controller has cancelled the pass on application` IS FALSE
    `my immigration pass has expired without renewal or been cancelled` IS FALSE

`a pass for a different occupation, approved` MEANS `My work pass` WITH
    `I hold a work pass issued to me` IS TRUE
    `the pass names as my employer the person I work for` IS TRUE
    `the work is in the trade, sector, occupation or type of employment specified in the pass or submitted in the application` IS FALSE
    `if the Controller has approved me to engage in this other work` IS TRUE
    `the period specified in the pass has not ended` IS TRUE
    `the Controller has suspended or revoked the pass` IS FALSE
    `the Controller has cancelled the pass on application` IS FALSE
    `my immigration pass has expired without renewal or been cancelled` IS FALSE

`a pass for a different occupation, not approved` MEANS `My work pass` WITH
    `I hold a work pass issued to me` IS TRUE
    `the pass names as my employer the person I work for` IS TRUE
    `the work is in the trade, sector, occupation or type of employment specified in the pass or submitted in the application` IS FALSE
    `if the Controller has approved me to engage in this other work` IS FALSE
    `the period specified in the pass has not ended` IS TRUE
    `the Controller has suspended or revoked the pass` IS FALSE
    `the Controller has cancelled the pass on application` IS FALSE
    `my immigration pass has expired without renewal or been cancelled` IS FALSE

`a pass whose immigration pass lapsed` MEANS `My work pass` WITH
    `I hold a work pass issued to me` IS TRUE
    `the pass names as my employer the person I work for` IS TRUE
    `the work is in the trade, sector, occupation or type of employment specified in the pass or submitted in the application` IS TRUE
    `if the Controller has approved me to engage in this other work` IS FALSE
    `the period specified in the pass has not ended` IS TRUE
    `the Controller has suspended or revoked the pass` IS FALSE
    `the Controller has cancelled the pass on application` IS FALSE
    `my immigration pass has expired without renewal or been cancelled` IS TRUE

`a revoked pass` MEANS `My work pass` WITH
    `I hold a work pass issued to me` IS TRUE
    `the pass names as my employer the person I work for` IS TRUE
    `the work is in the trade, sector, occupation or type of employment specified in the pass or submitted in the application` IS TRUE
    `if the Controller has approved me to engage in this other work` IS FALSE
    `the period specified in the pass has not ended` IS TRUE
    `the Controller has suspended or revoked the pass` IS TRUE
    `the Controller has cancelled the pass on application` IS FALSE
    `my immigration pass has expired without renewal or been cancelled` IS FALSE

`a cancelled pass` MEANS `My work pass` WITH
    `I hold a work pass issued to me` IS TRUE
    `the pass names as my employer the person I work for` IS TRUE
    `the work is in the trade, sector, occupation or type of employment specified in the pass or submitted in the application` IS TRUE
    `if the Controller has approved me to engage in this other work` IS FALSE
    `the period specified in the pass has not ended` IS TRUE
    `the Controller has suspended or revoked the pass` IS FALSE
    `the Controller has cancelled the pass on application` IS TRUE
    `my immigration pass has expired without renewal or been cancelled` IS FALSE

`no pass at all` MEANS `My work pass` WITH
    `I hold a work pass issued to me` IS FALSE
    `the pass names as my employer the person I work for` IS FALSE
    `the work is in the trade, sector, occupation or type of employment specified in the pass or submitted in the application` IS FALSE
    `if the Controller has approved me to engage in this other work` IS FALSE
    `the period specified in the pass has not ended` IS FALSE
    `the Controller has suspended or revoked the pass` IS FALSE
    `the Controller has cancelled the pass on application` IS FALSE
    `my immigration pass has expired without renewal or been cancelled` IS FALSE

`a careless work permit holder` MEANS `The circumstances` WITH
    `my pass` IS `a work permit for other work`
    `the damage or loss was caused by my negligence` IS TRUE
    `if the Controller permits otherwise` IS FALSE
    `I consented in writing to bear it` IS FALSE

`a careful work permit holder` MEANS `The circumstances` WITH
    `my pass` IS `a work permit for other work`
    `the damage or loss was caused by my negligence` IS FALSE
    `if the Controller permits otherwise` IS FALSE
    `I consented in writing to bear it` IS FALSE

`an S pass holder who consented, with the Controller's permission` MEANS `The circumstances` WITH
    `my pass` IS `an S pass`
    `the damage or loss was caused by my negligence` IS FALSE
    `if the Controller permits otherwise` IS TRUE
    `I consented in writing to bear it` IS TRUE

`an S pass holder who did not consent, with the Controller's permission` MEANS `The circumstances` WITH
    `my pass` IS `an S pass`
    `the damage or loss was caused by my negligence` IS FALSE
    `if the Controller permits otherwise` IS TRUE
    `I consented in writing to bear it` IS FALSE

`a careless miscellaneous work pass holder` MEANS `The circumstances` WITH
    `my pass` IS `a miscellaneous work pass`
    `the damage or loss was caused by my negligence` IS TRUE
    `if the Controller permits otherwise` IS FALSE
    `I consented in writing to bear it` IS FALSE

§ `s 2 -- who I am under the Act`

#ASSERT `Am I a foreigner under the Act` `a foreign worker`
#ASSERT NOT `Am I a foreigner under the Act` `a permanent resident at work`

-- A foreigner working for himself under no contract of service is a self-employed foreigner, not a foreign employee.
#ASSERT `Am I a foreign employee` `a foreign worker`
#ASSERT NOT `Am I a foreign employee` `a foreign freelance designer`

#ASSERT `Am I a self-employed foreigner` `a foreign freelance designer`

§ `s 12 -- is my pass valid`

-- Another employer is outside the pass; another occupation is inside it only with the Controller's approval;
-- an immigration pass that lapses takes the work pass with it (reg 2(3)).
#ASSERT `Is my work pass valid for this work for this employer` `my valid pass`
#ASSERT NOT `Is my work pass valid for this work for this employer` `a pass naming another employer`
#ASSERT `Is my work pass valid for this work for this employer` `a pass for a different occupation, approved`
#ASSERT NOT `Is my work pass valid for this work for this employer` `a pass whose immigration pass lapsed`

§ `ss 5(2), 10(1) -- am I breaking the law by working`

#ASSERT NOT `Am I breaking section 5(2) by working for this employer` `a foreign worker` `my valid pass`
#ASSERT `Am I breaking section 5(2) by working for this employer` `a foreign worker` `a pass for a different occupation, not approved`
#ASSERT NOT `Am I breaking section 5(2) by working for this employer` `a permanent resident at work` `no pass at all`

#ASSERT `Am I breaking section 10(1) by working for myself` `a foreign freelance designer` `no pass at all`

§ `ss 5(7), 10(2), 22 -- what I can be punished with`

#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined for` `being in employment without a valid work pass` FALSE EQUALS 20000
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined for` `not reporting the loss of my work pass within 7 days` FALSE EQUALS 10000

-- A late loss report is a fine-only offence (s 22(1)(g), (j)); being in employment without a valid pass, 2 years (s 5(7)).
#ASSERT `What is the longest I can be imprisoned for, in months` `being in employment without a valid work pass` FALSE EQUALS 24

-- A second s 10 conviction carries at least one month in prison (s 10(2)(b)).
#ASSERT `What is the shortest imprisonment I must get, in months` `being a self-employed foreigner without a valid work pass` TRUE EQUALS 1

-- s 27: the lower of half the maximum fine and 5,000. 20,000 / 2 = 10,000, so 5,000; 6,000 / 2 = 3,000.
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be asked to pay to compound my offence` `being in employment without a valid work pass` FALSE EQUALS 5000

#ASSERT `the most a composition can cost for an offence whose maximum fine is` 6000 EQUALS 3000

§ `s 21 -- arrest`

-- s 21(1) lists s 5(7) but not s 22(1)(b) (failing to produce the pass on demand).
#ASSERT `Can I be arrested without a warrant if suspected of` `being in employment without a valid work pass`
#ASSERT NOT `Can I be arrested without a warrant if suspected of` `not producing my work pass on demand`

#ASSERT `Have I been held longer than the Act allows` `an employment inspector` 49 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Have I been held longer than the Act allows` `a police officer` 72 EQUALS NOTHING

§ `ss 22A, 23A, 25(4), 25(6), regs 17, 18 -- what my employer may take from me`

#ASSERT `What does the Act say about my employer taking this from me` `the levy or a penalty on it` `a careless work permit holder` EQUALS `my employer must bear it, and taking it from me exposes my employer to a financial penalty`
#ASSERT `What does the Act say about my employer taking this from me` `a fee for getting the job` `a careless work permit holder` EQUALS `taking it is an offence`

-- Reg 17: a duplicate fee for a damaged pass is recoverable only if I was negligent; the fee for a second lost pass
-- is not listed, and the miscellaneous work pass has no duplicate fee at all.
#ASSERT `What does the Act say about my employer taking this from me` `a duplicate pass fee for a damaged pass` `a careless work permit holder` EQUALS `it may lawfully be taken from me`
#ASSERT `What does the Act say about my employer taking this from me` `a duplicate pass fee for a damaged pass` `a careful work permit holder` EQUALS `my employer must bear it, and taking it from me exposes my employer to a financial penalty`
#ASSERT `What does the Act say about my employer taking this from me` `a duplicate pass fee for a second or later replacement of a lost pass` `a careless work permit holder` EQUALS `my employer must bear it, and taking it from me exposes my employer to a financial penalty`
#ASSERT `What does the Act say about my employer taking this from me` `a duplicate pass fee for a damaged pass` `a careless miscellaneous work pass holder` EQUALS `my employer must bear it, and taking it from me exposes my employer to a financial penalty`

-- Reg 18: for an S pass the Controller's permission shifts repatriation only with my written consent; once shifted, it
-- is outside s 22A(3)(a), and on the literal words presumed to be for my employment.
#ASSERT `What does the Act say about my employer taking this from me` `my repatriation` `an S pass holder who consented, with the Controller's permission` EQUALS `taking it is presumed an offence until the taker proves otherwise`
#ASSERT `What does the Act say about my employer taking this from me` `my repatriation` `an S pass holder who did not consent, with the Controller's permission` EQUALS `my employer must bear it, and taking it from me exposes my employer to a financial penalty`

#ASSERT `What does the Act say about my employer taking this from me` `a salary deduction the Employment Act or my terms of employment allow` `a careless work permit holder` EQUALS `it may lawfully be taken from me`
#ASSERT `What does the Act say about my employer taking this from me` `some other sum` `a careless work permit holder` EQUALS `taking it is presumed an offence until the taker proves otherwise`

-- Seventh Schedule items 1(e) and 1(f): 65.40 and 109.
#ASSERT `How much of a duplicate pass fee can my employer recover from me` `a duplicate pass fee for a damaged pass` `a careless work permit holder` EQUALS JUST 65.40
#ASSERT `How much of a duplicate pass fee can my employer recover from me` `a duplicate pass fee for the first replacement of a lost pass` `a careless work permit holder` EQUALS JUST 109
#ASSERT `How much of a duplicate pass fee can my employer recover from me` `a duplicate pass fee for a second or later replacement of a lost pass` `a careless work permit holder` EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT `If the taker is convicted, what must the court order the taker to pay` 4500 EQUALS 4500

§ `s 9 -- when my pass is suspended or revoked`

#ASSERT `Within how many days of being notified must my employer end my employment` `a revoked pass` EQUALS JUST 7

#ASSERT NOT `Can I take the ending of my employment to my union or a trade dispute` `a revoked pass`

-- s 9(1) as a duty: ending the employment on day 5 of the 7 fulfils it.
#TRACE `my employer's duty to end my employment after revocation` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `my employer` DOES `end my employment` AT 5

§ `s 14 -- a lost pass`

#ASSERT `Did I report my lost work pass in time` 7

-- s 14(1) as a duty: reporting on day 3 fulfils it.
#TRACE `my duty to report a lost work pass` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `me` DOES `report the loss, destruction or defacement of my work pass to the Controller` AT 3

§ `s 11 -- the levy`

#ASSERT `Who must pay the levy on my work pass` `a foreign worker` EQUALS `my employer`
#ASSERT `Who must pay the levy on my work pass` `a foreign freelance designer` EQUALS `I do`

-- My stopping work is not on the s 11(2) list.
#ASSERT `Is the levy on my work pass still payable` `my valid pass` TRUE

-- s 11(5): 30% of 1,000 is 300, which caps a 500 penalty.
#ASSERT `What is the most late-payment penalty I can be charged on unpaid levy` 500 1000 EQUALS 300

§ `ss 5, 6, 6A, 22B -- what the person who employs me risks`

#ASSERT `What is the least fine the person who employed me must get` `employing me without a valid work pass` TRUE FALSE EQUALS 5000

-- s 5(6)(b): a repeat individual must be jailed for at least a month; a repeat company cannot be jailed but
-- faces up to 60,000.
#ASSERT `What is the most the person who employed me can be fined` `employing me without a valid work pass` TRUE TRUE EQUALS 30000
#ASSERT `What is the most the person who employed me can be fined` `employing me without a valid work pass` FALSE TRUE EQUALS 60000

#ASSERT `What is the shortest imprisonment the person who employed me must get, in months` `employing me without a valid work pass` TRUE TRUE EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `What is the shortest imprisonment the person who employed me must get, in months` `obtaining a work pass for me for a phantom business and not employing me` TRUE FALSE EQUALS 6

-- s 5(5): no due diligence without checking the passport.
#ASSERT `Can the person who employed me rely on not knowing I was a foreigner` TRUE TRUE TRUE

#ASSERT `Is the occupier of the premises where I am found presumed to have employed me` `a foreign worker` TRUE

#ASSERT `Must the occupier keep me out of the construction work place` `no pass at all` TRUE TRUE

-- s 6A(3): checking my original work pass is one of three alternative routes (an inference from the 'or').
#ASSERT `Can the occupier rebut the presumptions by not knowing I was a foreigner` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE

-- s 22B(2): more than 5 charged and at least 6 convicted at one trial.
#ASSERT `What extra punishment must the person who obtained phantom passes get` 6 6 FALSE EQUALS `caning`

#ASSERT `What is the most financial penalty the Controller can impose on my employer for` `not ending my employment within 7 days of revocation` EQUALS 10000
#ASSERT `What is the most financial penalty the Controller can impose on my employer for` `inadvertently giving the Controller inaccurate information` EQUALS 20000

§ `ss 25(2), 25C, 25G -- the Controller's penalties on me and my appeal`

#ASSERT `What is the most financial penalty the Controller can impose on me for` `breaching a regulatory condition of my work pass` EQUALS 10000

#ASSERT NOT `Can I be represented by a lawyer or paid agent before the Controller`

#ASSERT `Is my appeal to the Appeal Board in time` 14

#ASSERT `Does my appeal hold off the Controller's determination` TRUE

